Third-party dependency licences
================================

This section lists the licences of the packages that saltext.sqlx imports or installs, taken from the REAL package
metadata (importlib.metadata: License-Expression, License field and Classifier entries) of the T11 test environment
(CPython 3.13, Salt 3008.5, SQLAlchemy 2.0.55, every extra installed). Nothing here was copied from documentation.

Declared dependencies (pyproject.toml):

  Package            Declared as            Licence (package metadata)
  salt               salt>=3006             Apache Software License | Apache Software License 2.0  [3008.5]
  SQLAlchemy         SQLAlchemy>=2.0,<2.1   MIT  [2.0.55]
  pg8000             extra postgres         BSD-3-Clause (metadata: "BSD 3-Clause License")  [1.31.6]
  psycopg            extra postgres-psycopg LGPL-3.0-only  [3.3.6]
  PyMySQL            extra mysql            MIT  [1.2.3]
  oracledb           extra oracle           UPL-1.0 OR Apache-2.0  [26.1.0]
  pymssql            extra mssql            GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 (licence text in metadata)  [2.4.6]

  pg8000 installs scramp (MIT-0), which installs asn1crypto (MIT), and python-dateutil (BSD / Apache-2.0 dual licence).
  psycopg[binary] also installs psycopg-binary (LGPL-3.0-only, the compiled wheel of the same project).

LGPL notice. psycopg, psycopg-binary (the optional PostgreSQL driver, extra postgres-psycopg; the default driver pg8000 is BSD-3)
and pymssql (SQL Server driver) are licensed under the GNU
Lesser General Public License. The project owner accepted them on 2026-10-29 on one condition: they are used as
unmodified pip packages. saltext.sqlx imports them lazily through their public API, does not copy, vendor, patch or
statically link any of their code, and each can be replaced by the user with another build of the same package. Any
other LGPL package, and any GPL or AGPL package (for example mysqlclient, which is why PyMySQL is the MySQL driver),
fails tests/security/test_licences.py. No GPL package is present.

Notes on entries that are not plain permissive licences:
  certifi        MPL-2.0 (file-level copyleft; used unmodified; required by salt and requests)
  tempora        the package metadata declares no licence at all (no field, classifier or licence file); it is
                 required by portend, which CherryPy requires, which Salt requires (not by saltext.sqlx itself)

